title: Revolt of the Bolshevik Moderates
subtitle: They have issued their ultimatum. 
new-page: true
view-if: year = 1917 and month = 11 and week = 2 and moderate_strength > 20 and moderate_dissent > 20 and lenin_anger >= 1
max-visits: 1
tags: event

= Revolt of the Bolshevik Moderates

Feeling strongly about the need for compromise in order to stabilize and save the Revolution, and chaffing against the constraints Lenin has placed upon them, the leaders of the Bolshevik Moderates have threatened to resign from the Central Committee and their various government offices. This they feel will finally communicate to the Leninists the severity of the situation, and grant them the freedom to properly express their views before the Party masses. 

Needless to say, the loss of some of our Party's best leaders will severely set back our government.  

>• Those who will resign immediately: Kamenev, Rykov, Zinoviev, Nogin, Milyutin, Teodorovich, Riazanov, Larin (and several others).<br>
>• Those who lodge their severe protest (but do not resign): Shliapnikov, Lozovsky 

- @let_them_resign
- @assuage


