The Moderates resign from their posts. While hoping this act of defiance will rally support for their side within the Party, it also limits their influence. Meanwhile, critics and moderate socialists take this affair as proof the Bolsheviks are starting to disintegrate. 

@assuage
title: Is there no way to assuage the Moderates?

- @compromise
- @congress
- @let_them_right: On second thought, let them resign. 

@compromise
title: Discuss a compromise solution.
choose-if: lenin_anger < 2
unavailable-subtitle: Tensions are too high to consider this. 

@congress
title: Call Lenin's bluff and demand a Party Congress to litigate the issue. 
choose-if: moderate_strength >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: The Moderates lack the strength to consider this. 
on-arrival: party_congress_timer = 8 if party_congress_timer > 8; moderate_strength += 5; moderate_dissent += 10; 

Rather than resigning, the Moderates instead force through the convening of a Party Congress. Now both sides will have the opportunity to campaign in support of their respective views, and have their case heard before representatives of the Party at-large. 
